                            <comment id="16752590" author="githubbot" created="Fri, 25 Jan 2019 19:11:49 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;rdblue commented on pull request #603: &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/PARQUET-1510&quot; title=&quot;Dictionary filter skips null values when evaluating not-equals.&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;PARQUET-1510&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;PARQUET-1510&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;: Fix notEq for optional columns with null values.&lt;br/&gt;
URL: &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/parquet-mr/pull/603&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://github.com/apache/parquet-mr/pull/603&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;


&lt;p&gt;   Dictionaries cannot contain null values, so notEq filters cannot&lt;br/&gt;
   conclude that a block cannot match using only the dictionary. Instead,&lt;br/&gt;
   it must also check whether the block may have at least one null value.&lt;br/&gt;
   If there are no null values, then the existing check is correct.&lt;/p&gt;

